WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.962
This workbook's own governance design
already says what this pipeline must produce.

2
00:00:04.962 --> 00:00:08.300
These are the workbook's rules,
not an external standard.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.925
Drift is measured against a
versioned record, not a snapshot.

4
00:00:11.925 --> 00:00:14.737
No closure counts unless
it carries its proof.

5
00:00:14.737 --> 00:00:19.275
And a finding closes only when a later
observation shows the fixed state.

6
00:00:19.275 --> 00:00:21.837
The pipeline is a small
part of that design.

7
00:00:21.837 --> 00:00:25.862
Each validation kit check compares
the tenant with the program's record.

8
00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:29.825
The pipeline compares this run with
the last, and that finds change.

9
00:00:29.825 --> 00:00:33.475
Whether a change is drift from the
record is still the check's answer.

10
00:00:33.475 --> 00:00:36.319
A finding that was there
yesterday and is still

11
00:00:36.319 --> 00:00:38.725
there today isn't new,
but it is still open.

12
00:00:38.725 --> 00:00:42.148
And the comparison enforces
the closing rule in code:

13
00:00:42.148 --> 00:00:47.500
a check that ended in Error proves nothing,
so its findings stay open as unverified.
